<tei:p><tei:pb n="614" ed="1949 festival musaf" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n638_medium.jpg"/><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:regalim/musaf/text/umipnei"/>Because of our sins we were exiled from our country and banished far from our land. We cannot go up as pilgrims to worship thee, to perform our duties in thy chosen House, the great and holy Temple which was called by thy name, on account of the hand that was let loose on thy sanctuary. May it be thy will, Lord our God and God of our fathers, merciful King, in thy abundant love <tei:pb n="616" ed="1949 festival musaf" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n640_medium.jpg"/>again to have mercy on us and on thy sanctuary; rebuild it speedily and magnify its glory.<tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
    </tei:body>
